# Files where the port differs on inputs that select the self-host CI jobs.
# First mismatches in the measured baseline: scoped count / whole-tree count.
# Program-changing: semicolon-separated statements concatenated (0 / 2).
# Program-changing: case branches joined (0 / 3).
# Program-changing: macro text loses end (1 / 1).
# Assignment and enum alignment (10 / 17).
# Multiline collections collapsed (8 / 18).
# Multiline calls or declarations collapsed (3 / 6).
# Multiline boolean expressions collapsed (1 / 2).
# Missing space after a proc literal opening brace (2 / 3).
# Extra space in empty blocks (0 / 2).
# Inline comment alignment lost (3 / 7).
# Inline comments moved to a new line (3 / 3).
# Indentation changed (1 / 3).
# Newly accepted: macro branch indentation, inline comment alignment and moved enum comments.
# #217's semantic fixtures, new files never on the floor, whose subject is a construct the port prints
# differently: `b.@v` printed as `b`; `{ a; b }` printed as `{ ab }`; `-> { x }` printed as `-> {x }`;
# an `x = if` body indented two spaces instead of under the `if`; blank lines in an enum body dropped;
# valued enum members' `=` not aligned.
